{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein","title":"rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.md","line":204,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex#rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","label":"rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein","line":380,"source":"\\begin{remark}[constant curvature is Einstein]\n  \\label{rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0104}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature, def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold, prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation}\n\n  \\sketch\n  If $(M,g)$ has constant curvature $k$, it is Einstein with Einstein constant\n  $(n-1)k$: for unit $v$, \\cref{prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation} gives\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v,v)=\\sum_{i=2}^n\\sec(v,e_i)=(n-1)k$.\n\\end{remark}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Remark</div></section>[constant curvature is Einstein] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368332d636f6e7374616e742d6375727661747572652d65696e737465696e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0104</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-constant-curvature\">↗ def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-einstein-manifold\">↗ def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation\">↗ prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation</a> <p></p>\\sketch If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> has constant curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span>, it is Einstein with Einstein constant <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n-1)k$\">$(n-1)k$</span>: for unit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span>, <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368332d72696363692d73656374696f6e616c2d72656c6174696f6e\">subsection 1.4</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)=\\sum _{i=2}^n\\sec (v,e_i)=(n-1)k$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)=\\sum _{i=2}^n\\sec (v,e_i)=(n-1)k$</span>. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-ricci-determines-sec-low-dim","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-einstein-not-constant-curvature-examples","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature","label":"def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold","title":"def:pet-ch3-einstein-manif